  "notes": "Drawn from 2024-25 photos of a 787-9 (measured), an A321neo and a 787-10/767. The Triton Blue band is level with the windows aft of the wing (the windows sit in it), and below them ahead of the wing. Belly not seen squarely: white, as the lower sides show. Not drawn: the registration, the type ('BOEING 787-9') and a small flag by the aft door. The sharklets' inner face wasn't seen. Some 777s and 787s carry 'Inspiration of JAPAN'; it is fleet-wide by 2025 photos. Many specials (Star Wars, Pokémon, the A380 'Flying Honu' turtles, Star Alliance) are not this scheme. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on JA936A: title lengths measured (ANA 0.043, the slogan 0.124, its lowercase 0.66 of its capitals; the fin's ANA runs about 0.7 of the chord where it starts); the two bands' edges are sweeping curves, now drawn smooth through the measured points.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Triton Blue has been ANA's standard since 1982-83, replacing the Mohican scheme (light-blue cheatline and a stylised Leonardo helicopter on the fin)."
